@@ -95,3 +95,97 @@ argv = [
 # what it does when it runs out of allocator. A `fatal_output_substrings` policy
 # would replace the process at the first marker and the pass would measure the
 # replacement instead of the failure.
+
+# A third candidate: `llama-server` from the pinned Homebrew `llama.cpp 0.3.0`,
+# build `b10621-c1d0e7a00`.
+#
+# Every flag here is a condition `RuntimeBenchmark.contextPolicy` reads, and
+# each one is spelled the way this runtime spells it. None of them was added by
+# relaxing an admission clause.
+#
+# `--ctx-size` is NOT what pins the KV bound. This runtime has no unbounded
+# mode -- measured, it reports `n_ctx` 32768 from the model with no context flag
+# at all and 8192 under `--ctx-size 8192` -- so the bound is read from the
+# running server's `/v1/models` `meta.n_ctx` by the gate, inside its own
+# observation window. The flag is still stated because admission refuses a
+# launch that pins a bound the process did not honour: ask for 8192 and run
+# 4096 and the pair is refused by name. Match it to the baseline's
+# `--max-kv-size`, or the two contextPolicy pins will differ and the pair will
+# be refused for that instead -- which is the correct refusal, because a
+# 32k window and an unbounded one are not the same condition.
